+# box_spine.dem — v2-mechanics-the-box: the Box's arc on the REAL catalog
+# (era 1: 6 basic pieces, 240 standard tiles, no fiber; the clock spine at
+# 2400 ticks / 120 s per dot on the base interval). The beats:
+#
+#   400-800ms  — the player builds: the fixture leg + a second router +
+#                parallel segments (the spool visibly drains 240 -> ~180).
+#   116000ms   — PRE-dot capture: the box drained (stock < cap).
+#   120000+    — tick 2400: the DOT fires — stock restores TO cap (never
+#                past), the BOX_DOT event rides the T1 hash.
+#   122000ms   — `advance 2`: the era-2 latch fires (gate off, no crisis) —
+#                the crazyhouse rule: caps RAISE (basic 8) and stock restores
+#                to the new ceiling (the era-2 restore beat, also in the T1).
+#   123000ms   — POST-dot + post-advance capture: the box refilled at the
+#                raised ceiling (glanceable HUD beat).
+#   124500ms   — settled era-2 beat (the network running at the new kit).
+#
+# `box on` (run setup — the r1 B1 rule: carried identically on the replay
+# path) arms the material economy; every draw/place/demolish/advance below
+# is a LOGGED command, replay-byte-identical (E10). The T1 pins the box
+# section (sparse stock + clock) from the first drained tick onward.
+seed 42
+era 1
+box on
+run 126000ms
+at 400ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 500ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 600ms place router_basic 30 8
+at 700ms draw 1 3 standard
+at 800ms draw 1 3 standard
+capture at 116000ms
+capture at 124500ms
+at 122000ms advance 2
+capture at 123000ms
+capture at 125000ms
+expect hash stable
